Main license: BSD-3-Clause. Bundled utilite: LGPL-3.0-or-later.
Private rtflann: BSD FLANN/LZ4-derived code; no second public provider.
OpenCV 5 patch: selected from accepted upstream PR1732 by Mathieu Labbe,
merge d9f3337f978fffd9cf4b04bee15636bf00a2b870; selection is local.
Other adaptations: EmberBSD, AI-assisted; not submitted or accepted upstream.
Dependency pins and headless includes preserve actual shared current APIs.
Stable GTSAM 4.3.0 uses AttitudeFactor<Pose3> and std::optional::has_value().
RVL codec: Andrew D. Wilson, Fast Lossless Depth Image Compression, SIGCHI'17,
MIT; its representative source notice and MIT license are installed.
Local corrections preserve aligned metadata access, defined RVL arithmetic,
bounded depth-image decoding, and private bundled LZ4 symbol visibility.
Utilite corrections cover atomic worker state, natural-completion/self-join,
and destruction of an unlocked mutex; they do not establish every API race-free.
Installed CMake exports resolve the common providers without build-host paths.
The resource generator is built for the host; BUILD_TOOLS=OFF omits its install.
Final destruction releases the owned marker detector and default strategies
recreated by close(); reusable close/init behavior remains covered separately.
Private KD-tree leaf nodes initialize the split value before serialization;
the saved-index format and common public FLANN provider remain unchanged.
POSIX workers are joinable: join waits for OS termination including TLS cleanup,
and start reaps an earlier completed worker before reuse. Windows is unchanged.
Raw thread handles/IDs remain creator-owned until successful join; synchronize
their getters externally. No UThread fields, size, alignment or signatures change.
